    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "A maximum distortional strain energy density criterion (D-criterion) is proposed for shear fracture propagation. Using a displacement discontinuity boundary element method, the propagation paths of two echelon shear fractures are simulated by applying the newly proposed criterion. It is shown that echelon mode-II shear fractures always propagate toward each other regardless of sense of shear or fault step direction. Although the simulation is done for an idealized non-porous elastic solid, the predicted shear fracture paths agree well with the field observations.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
